ignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-65-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1064019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d1c93938ff62f41945b1feb10428c4e6195c33f365f1608bde48be838bbd2831","compact":"ff122eaecdd43b60d6a5e8ba295d82a78088d0588b50b018779b9ad109cfb72f","nasal":"ff122eaecdd43b60d6a5e8ba295d82a78088d0588b50b018779b9ad109cfb72f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-64-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":64,"verse":20,"english":"This, O Rāma, is the foremost of ascetics, this one is Asceticism incarnate. This one ever abide by duty; and he is the stay of ascetic energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-65-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1064020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b4127eb944a611389ff6b7b89629d814a2054cb64b3b3c9ba76bae75db157b04","compact":"78af5615dbbcf7fd5e3477a888b114e72c1d30044f1be5811f12dd1767ec9cd5","nasal":"78af5615dbbcf7fd5e3477a888b114e72c1d30044f1be5811f12dd1767ec9cd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-64-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":64,"verse":21,"english":"Having said this, that best of regenerate persons paused. Hearing Satānanda's narration delivered in the presence of Rāma and Laks maņa, Janaka with clasped hands addressed the son of Kusika.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-65-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1064021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f392d0c54c385a0f06505e7e6bb5ad34a3c66102cb321d3574045fe02be69d4","compact":"0ac8797c3f2e302b365f3ea0bddebf27094dad57d90cc37bdeb2978e403143a7","nasal":"3a576ac2983abeff78b68e08d0e5c0043dcf236c99c55a622e16a86681bfd63b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-64-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala",